                            {
                                "target_word": "peeled",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "797f0fd5-0fba-3f29-9ce3-76030038d80f",
                                        "entry_id": "f7a96a9a-ce0c-3fd8-8301-88bc8bf739aa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a peel; (in combination) having the specified type of peel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf9f30c1-c8cd-4a57-b01d-160d1aa55b8c",
                                                "sense_id": "797f0fd5-0fba-3f29-9ce3-76030038d80f",
                                                "text": "Genova lemons average 8-10 sections and 5-6 seeds. They are thick-peeled and acid. Thin-peeled fruit at right was cured about 10 days."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6718ab4-e541-49e8-b4a4-abb5bd5f2444",
                                                "sense_id": "797f0fd5-0fba-3f29-9ce3-76030038d80f",
                                                "text": "Only some mammals, such as monkeys (Janson, 1983) and bats (Phua and Corlett, 1989), appear to have the necessary dental capacity to open peeled fruits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c563134b-1fae-4bcb-98ae-ffc8106fc068",
                                                "sense_id": "797f0fd5-0fba-3f29-9ce3-76030038d80f",
                                                "text": "We don’t know who Foster is, but he sure hates bananas. This New Orleans classic takes the nutritious yellow-peeled fruit, drowns it in butter, smothers it with sugar, douses it with rum, and sets it on fire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c285885-b8d6-49a2-866f-e1ec854d3cb5",
                                                "sense_id": "797f0fd5-0fba-3f29-9ce3-76030038d80f",
                                                "text": "Transmittance mode can help to gather information about the constituents of thick-peeled fruit (e.g., citrus fruit, cantaloupes, melons), however these measurements require very high light intensities, which could result in burning of fruit surface and the alteration of spectral information."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
